course: dictionary
lesson: 64
title: One word, many meanings: acid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The noun acid is a chemical that tastes sour, and strong acids can burn skin. «Lemon juice and vinegar are weak acids, safe to taste.» The sentence is about food, so acid means a sour chemical.
explain: Acid can also be an adjective, acidic, meaning containing acid or tasting sour. Look at what is being described. «Carbon steel knives get dark spots when left wet with acid such as vinegar.» Here acid names the chemical that causes the spots.
explain: Acid can even describe words. An acid remark is sharp and unkind, not a chemical at all. Ask yourself: is this about a substance, or about how someone speaks? The words around it give the answer, just as they do for any new word.
fact: An acid is a chemical substance that tastes sour.
fact: Strong acids can burn skin and dissolve metals, so never touch or taste chemicals.
fact: The pH scale measures acids (below 7), neutral (7) and alkalis (above 7).
fact: «Acid rain» damages trees and buildings.
fact: «Acid test» means a real test of something.
exercise: «Plaque is a sticky film of bacteria on teeth; they make acid that slowly dissolves the enamel.» What does the acid do to teeth? | It makes teeth shine like new | *It slowly dissolves the enamel and makes holes | It keeps germs away from the teeth | It helps teeth grow stronger
exercise: Asha says «an acid remark» means a kind, soft comment. What does it really mean? | A very long comment | A gentle, sweet comment | *A sharp, unkind comment | A comment written in ink
exercise: Which of these is a weak acid that is safe to eat? | Sulphuric acid | *Lemon juice | Battery acid | Hydrochloric acid
test: «Vultures have strong stomach acid that kills germs.» What job does the stomach acid do? | It helps the vulture fly faster | It makes its feathers grow | It cools the vulture's body down | *It kills germs that would make the vulture ill
test: Scientists use red cabbage water or litmus paper to find acids. How does the test show an acid? | *It changes colour | It makes a loud noise | It turns invisible | It gets much heavier
exam: In «He gave an acid reply and walked off», what does acid mean? | Bright and shiny | *Sharp and unkind | Cold and wet | A sour chemical from a lab
